{
  "title": "A stale commit that records a conflict",
  "description": "A separate story from the Acme quote. Sam's agent read dossier 20 for a Globex discount: nothing stood in the way, so at 10:02 it approved a 15% discount. At 10:05 finance froze discounts above 10%, and memory produced dossier 21 with a new constraint. Sam's agent then reports against dossier 20. Memory records nothing, says dossier 21 is current, and includes the update the agent may have missed. The agent commits again against dossier 21, listing the constraint its action went against. Memory records the claim and routes the conflict to a person. Because a commit's conflicts may only name items of the dossier it is based on, refusing the stale commit is what gets the freeze in front of a person.",
